{"user": "is it possible to flip tokens if there's a gap? Imagine white played B8, would they still flip the black tokens in row b?", "user_ts": "2026-08-05T13:21:39.370812+00:00", "assistant": "No \u2014 you **cannot flip across a gap**.\n\nFlips only happen in a **continuous straight line** of opponent discs, ending with one of your own discs. An empty square breaks the line.\n\nSo if **White played b8**, they would **not** flip up column **b**, because **b7** and **b6** are empty gaps.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-05T13:21:44.607296+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-05T13:21:45.696668+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Negative Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Negative Feedback": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Negative Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "Gene